{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"TRIAGE RECORD + a correction to my own earlier reading.\n\nRe-scoped this ticket to the one defect that survives investigation: the Verified -1 message carries no triage signal. The two refuted premises are preserved in the comments above — (1) the concurrency group is not keyed per change (refuted: the group already keys on GERRIT_CHANGE_ID, and only ONE job was cancelled per run where a concurrency cancel would kill all of them), and (2) all-shards selection exceeds timeout-minutes 30 (refuted: fixed on main by ac0f62be's per-shard parallel matrix — run 31563668309 selected all 7 shards and all 7 passed, worst 20m22s of a 30m budget).\n\n## Correction\n\nI earlier reported the 'select mutation shards' step failing with 'fatal: couldn't find remote ref refs/changes/25/1625/1'. That was a misread: those log lines were cyan-highlighted ECHO of the step's own script source — the checkout action's embedded default error string — not its output. The actual failure is\n\n    mutation_gate.py: error: argument command: invalid choice: 'select' (choose from run, smoke)\n\nThis is version skew, not a live defect. The reusable workflow resolves at main's ref and calls the new 'select' subcommand, while those runs execute scripts/mutation_gate.py from a patchset checkout based BEFORE ac0f62be added it. A rebase fixes it; 1625 is being rebased. No new ticket.\n\n## Why this strengthens the remaining defect\n\nIt is a second, completely different cause producing the same uninformative vote. Compare what Gerrit showed for each:\n\n| runs | actual cause | Gerrit message |\n|---|---|---|\n| 31560638673, 31562494026 | mutation job hit timeout-minutes: 30 | CANCELLED: <url> |\n| 31563192064, 31563305610 | selector step: invalid choice 'select' (version skew) | CANCELLED: <url> |\n\nA timeout on a healthy patchset and a stale-base version skew are indistinguishable from the vote. The first needs no author action, the second needs a rebase — and the message tells an agent neither. That is precisely what the re-scoped work fixes.\n\n## Design constraint found while scoping\n\nlfreleng-actions/gerrit-review-action hardcodes its message as \"${STATUS}: <run url>\" and exposes no input for custom text. I verified this at the pinned SHA a1c036a5 (v1.1.2) and on the action's current main, and v1.1.2 is the latest tag — so there is no upstream bump available. The detail must therefore be posted as an additional comment-only review rather than by enriching the vote message in place. Vote semantics are untouched.\n\n## Conflict check vs change 1627\n\n1627 ('Skip mutation gate for pre-gate patchsets', status NEW) touches .github/workflows/_mutation.yml and tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py. My change touches gerrit-verify.yaml, a new scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py, and a new tests/scripts/ test. No file overlap; I will not touch either of 1627's files."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786513355187084001,"uuid":"48c27ff0-27ef-4f13-80b0-95a4872945d7"}